# t59:
name: 1 ref, 2 gz pair with empty gzip members, issue 466
info: |
  Regression test for issue 466: the indexed gz feed (default '-readfeed 0') aborted with
    "The inflate wrapper offset (..) does not match the requested exact stop offset .."
  when a reads file contained an empty gzip member whose deflate stream is a single empty
  stored block '01 00 00 ff ff' (written by libdeflate for empty input e.g. fastp output).
  The reads are set4_mate_pairs_metatranscriptomics_[1|2].fastq recompressed as multi-member gzip,
  500 reads per member, with an empty stored-block member after every 2nd member.
  Generated with test_data/refs/scripts/gen_empty_member_gz.py:
    gen_empty_member_gz.py set4_mate_pairs_metatranscriptomics_1.fastq \
      set4_mate_pairs_metatranscriptomics_1_empty_member.fastq.gz 1 500 stored 2
  Outputs must equal those of '-readfeed 1' on the same input.
      input type         |               output type                  |    alignment type
  refs  reads  zip  pair | pair_in  pair_out  out2  sout  zout  other | best  N  min_lis seeds
    1     2     1    1       1        0         1     0     1      1      1    1     2      2
args:
  -ref: [ {{ REF_DIR }}/silva-arc-16s-database-id95.fasta ]
  -reads:
    - {{ DATA_DIR if DATA_DIR }}/set4_mate_pairs_metatranscriptomics_1_empty_member.fastq.gz  # 5,000 reads
    - {{ DATA_DIR if DATA_DIR }}/set4_mate_pairs_metatranscriptomics_2_empty_member.fastq.gz  # 5,000 reads
  -fastx:
  -paired_in:
  -out2:
  -other:
  -v:
  -threads: '{{THREADS or 4}}'
  -workdir: {{ WRK_DIR }}
validate:
  func:
  variant: sanger  # fastq quality variant
  files:
    aligned.log:
      num_reads: 10000
      num_hits:   4078
      num_fail:   5922
    aligned_fwd.fq.gz: 3654  # paired_in
    aligned_rev.fq.gz: 3654
    other_fwd.fq.gz:   1346
    other_rev.fq.gz:   1346
